# Get a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys.
#
# LOCAL ONLY. Do not set this on the Vercel deployment: without it, no request
# to the deployed site can reach a provider, which is a stronger guarantee than
# any permission check in this repository. Runs are recorded here and published
# by committing public/runs/. Verify with ./verify-deployment.sh <url>.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...

# Your deployed URL. OpenRouter attributes free-tier usage to it.
# Leave unset locally.
# SITE_URL=https://clickgym.vercel.app

# Owner mode. Starting a run spends this deployment's model quota, so /api/agent
# is limited to whoever holds this passcode — and is closed to EVERYONE while it
# is unset, including locally. Without it the platform is read-only: the recorded
# runs are all still on the console, and the sign-in control hides itself rather
# than offering something that always fails.
#
# Set it to anything long and unguessable. It never reaches the browser; the
# cookie carries a hash of it, not the value.
OWNER_PASSCODE=
